$DIR/main.p:17:12: cannot return P{...}, which points into arr, a local array of mk
    P{...} points into arr. arr is a local array of mk (declared at main.p:14).
    Its memory is reclaimed when mk returns, so P{...} would point at memory
    that no longer holds arr.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Return values instead of views of arr, or allocate arr and return its owner,
    an owned[[1]func() int]:
        arr := new([1]func() int)
        ...
        return arr
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3001" for a longer explanation)
